{"text": "otscer _\n(b)(6) (b)(6)\n\nEDUCATION\nMaster\u2019s of Arts in Teaching . Lewis and Clark College Portland, OR\nAugust 1975\nBS in Communications Lewis and Clark College Portland, OR\nJune 1972\nEMPLOYMENT HIsTORY\nPrincipal, Parakletos Strategic Public Affairs, LLC.\nSalem, OR July 2010-present\n\n\u00a2 Serve a variety of private industry clients with targeted messaging and strategic advocacy in the\nareas of energy, financial services, capital construction and transportation.\n\nOregon State Senator, District 26\nOregon Legislature Salem, OR Jan, 1999- Jan.2011\ne Elected Senate President Pro-Tempore by Senate Colleagues in 2009\ne Chair, Senate Business and Transportation Committee 2003-2011\n\u00a9 Member of the following Senate Committees during career: Education and General Government,\nRules, Revenue, Judiciary, Human Services, Consumer Protection.\n\u00a9 Member of the Senate Leadership Team 2009-2011\n\u00a9 Chief sponsor of $B408 that rewrote utility regulation in Oregon to better protect consumers.\n\u00a9 Co-author of HB2001 in 2009 creating the greatest transportation investment in Oregon history.\n\nPrincipal, Metsger Forbes LLC Portland, OR June2004-Dec.2007\n\n\u00a9 Delivered strategic advocacy, marketing and communication presentations at numerous state\ncredit union association meetings throughout the United States.\n\u00a9 Served diverse client base of health care, financial services, insurance, & other companies with\nstrategic planning and execution needs.\n\nPrincipal, NewsMedia Dynamics Inc. Portland, OR Oct-1992-Dec.1999\n\u00a9 Developed and implemented strategic legislative, communication and marketing plans for a wide\ntange of public and private sector clients.\n* Focused on the evolutionary shaping of public opinion for clients by identifying the needs and\nconcerns of the client\u2019s multiple audiences to design strategies targeted at influencing behavior,\n* Maximized use of earned media opportunities by utilizing two decades of mass media experience\nin Oregon to achieve targeted results,\n\u00a9 Worked effectively with multiple government and Private sector entities to reach consensus on\ncomplex and sometimes controversial issues,\n\nExecutive Director, Oregon Film and Video Foundation\nPortland, OR 1995-1997 (est.)\n\u00a9 Developed and implemented successful fundraising efforts for the Foundation.",
